{
  "summary": "The fused softmax kernel configuration (fused=true) significantly improved performance by reducing kernel launches and intermediate memory traffic, confirming bottlenecks K05 (fusion) and K09 (launch overhead) as impactful. The median execution time dropped from about 0.04 ms to approximately 0.023 ms, achieving a speedup of ~1.75x over the incumbent. Resource usage remains low with no spills, validating that resource pressure (K04) is not a limiting factor. However, masking overhead (K07) due to irregular input shape remains a potential bottleneck unaddressed by this config. Memory coalescing (K01) and numerical stability (K10) are still uncertain but likely less critical given stable validation results. No source changes were needed to enable fusion, only configuration adjustment.",
  "failures": "No failures reported; the fused kernel passed validation and improved performance as expected. The remaining masking overhead due to non-multiple tile dimension sizes still causes some inefficiency.",
  "next_steps": [
    {
      "description": "Investigate masking overhead (K07) reduction strategies to improve boundary tile handling for irregular shapes.",
      "suggestion": "Experiment with padding input dimensions or adjusting block size to better align with input dimensions, balancing masking overhead and resource use."
    },
    {
      "description": "Explore memory coalescing (K01) improvements.",
      "suggestion": "Profile memory access patterns and consider layout transformations or lane-to-address mappings to reduce excess memory transactions."
    },
    {
      "description": "Evaluate alternative warp and stage configurations to potentially improve parallel reduction efficiency (K06).",
      "suggestion": "Test configurations with increased num_warps or num_stages to determine if reduction communication overhead can be better balanced."
    },
    {
      "description": "Consider enabling tensor cores if applicable to hardware and data type.",
      "suggestion": "Test configurations with tensor_core=true to leverage hardware acceleration, if supported."
    }
  ]
}

